stand-debian-md-ext4-bios — the REAL donor inventory captured by tools/migrator-test.sh
(phase capture) from the debian-md-ext4-bios fixture VM booted into the Live: Debian 11,
dos, 2x8 GiB virtio (vda, vdb), /boot ext4 on md0 (foreign homehost -> md126 in the Live,
metadata 1.2, data_offset 4096), swap on vda2 AND vdb2, / ext4 on md1 (md127, data_offset
10240), fstab by UUID, ifupdown on ens3. Recipient: the synthetic 960 GB virtio box.

Exercises the planner on inventory.sh's real output (not hand-written records): mdadm lists
the mirror members as "vdb1,vda1" -> the base disk must still be vda (the member disk that
sorts first, the order pc_slots walks); vdb1/vdb3 dropped as mirrors; vdb2 appended as an
extra swap slot (from-other-disk, renumbered 2->3); root elastic renumbered 3->4 on dos;
both /boot and / block with grow; mkswap lines carry the fixture's swap UUIDs and labels;
identity keeps all four UUID= specs; modalias-not-checked WARN (no pci_drivers in the
capture). Checked by hand against tests/fixtures/stand-debian-md-ext4-bios/donor.inv.
Re-capture with: bash tools/migrator-test.sh -p capture (writes donor.inv + raw/).
